                    "message": "I would avoid testing against `PLDM_SUCCESS` here. The API returns either 0 or a negative errno value, neither of which are intended as type `enum pldm_completion_codes`. It happens to be the case that `PLDM_SUCCESS` is defined as 0 by the spec, but that's a coincidence."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_fw_update_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 1370,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Mayank Metha D",
                        "email": "mayank.metha@intel.com",
                        "username": "mmetha"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_fw_update_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 1374,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "In general, if libpldm APIs return an error value then you mustn't assume that any out-parameters contain a decoded value."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_fw_update_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 1374,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Mayank Metha D",
                        "email": "mayank.metha@intel.com",
                        "username": "mmetha"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_fw_update_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 1389,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Why not use `struct pldm_fwup_update_security_revision_req` here directly?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_fw_update_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 1389,
